Phase 1 core checks passed:
- headless simulation does not import Tkinter
- contract v1.2/v1.3 tuning matches simulation constants
- pickup 10 motes and light a new lantern
- pulse cost, stun and score
- shade collision, health and dropped motes
- island edge fall damage
- loss at zero flames
- dawn below 60% lanterns is a loss
- dawn with 60% lanterns wins and scores dawn bonus
- same-seed deterministic JSONL output
- invalid input and scenario exit with code 2

Phase 2 core checks passed:
- contract v1.2/v1.3 matches simulation constants
- three maps contain required geometry and entities
- --night 1|2|3 runs
- invalid night exits 2
- pause increments tick but not sim_tick and freezes time
- dash moves faster than walking
- glide limits falling speed
- lost wisp pushes the player
- wind charm grants immunity and blocks wisp push
- strong wind pushes unless a charm is active
- fall loses a flame and respawns safely
- all lanterns lit does not win before dawn
- Night 3 wins at dawn without requiring the bell tower
- Night 3 dawn threshold is ceil(60% of 7) = 5
- Night 3 output is deterministic
- 21,600 Night 3 ticks finish in 0.87s
- godot/shared is in sync with contract and maps

Phase 3 core checks passed:
- contract v1.2 tuning, score and ui are in sync
- snapshot exposes fuel, ever_lit, capacity and dawn fields
- refuel uses the nearest receiving lantern
- refuel tie-break uses the smaller lantern id
- refuel only spends ceil(missing fuel / 10) motes
- full lantern rejects refuel without an event or score
- ambient drain depletes exactly at 60 ticks and emits lantern_out
- shade drain is 5/s and stops after the lantern goes out
- shade drain removes one fuel per 10 ticks below fuel 30
- shade chases the player from 10 m
- relight costs 5 motes, scores 50 and increments relit_count
- new light costs 10 motes, scores 100 and raises capacity to 12
- capacity is min(20, 10 + 2*lights) and resets each night
- refuel crossing fuel 30 pushes nearby shades
- refuel below fuel 30 does not push shades
- dawn win needs ceil(60%) and scores 500 + flames*50
- dawn below threshold is a loss
- no_flames takes precedence over the dawn result
- scoring has no time bonus and pays per surviving flame
- colorblind mode is persisted/echoed and validated
- fuel/drain simulation is deterministic
- 21,600 Night 3 fuel ticks finish in 0.66s
- godot/shared is in sync with contract and maps

